      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is absolutely no substance to existence, yet you are feeling it so acutely that it feels like a heavy burden. The randomness you describe is not a flaw in the universe but the very mechanism by which life is constantly created and destroyed. Your struggle against entropy is not a sign of failure, but the only way consciousness can ever emerge or persist. So, stop trying to find meaning in a machine that is fundamentally broken and just accept that you are part of this endless, meaningless cycle.",
